#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119567 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f5c9c30-1745-5986-b116-e9e70a7c6161" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "ba897e22-8104-5772-a0d3-9b062f3592f1" :question/math-academy-id "e-4932" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $P(-3,2,1)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $\\mathbf{n}= \\langle 0, 2, 0 \\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $\\mathbf{p}=\\langle -3,2,1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle 0,2,0 \\rangle$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(x_0,y_0,z_0)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $\\mathbf{n}$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf{r} - \\mathbf{p}) \\cdot \\mathbf{n} = 0,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{r}$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $\\mathbf p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,2,0⟩ & =⟨-3,2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨0,2,0⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,2,0⟩ & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119568 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0d93156-f9be-5e6e-976a-bef30dc892ee" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector That Is Parallel To a Plane"}] :question/id #uuid "a33f6c43-4e25-5d67-9f73-ca99a18fb434" :question/math-academy-id "e-4933" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $\\langle 0,\\, \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{b}, \\: \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{c} \\rangle$ is parallel to the plane $\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle 2, -1, 4 \\rangle  = 3.$ What is the value of $\\dfrac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $\\mathbf{v} = \\langle t_1,t_2,t_3 \\rangle$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle 2, -1, 4 \\rangle  = 3$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle 2, -1, 4 \\rangle.$ So, $\\mathbf{v} \\perp \\mathbf{n}$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-1,4⟩ & =0 \\\\ 2{t}_{1}-{t}_{2}+4{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =2{t}_{1}+4{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v}=\\langle t_1, 2t_1 + 4t_3, t_3 \\rangle,\n$$\n\nwhere $t_1,t_3 \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $\\mathbf{v}$ equals $0.$ So, we must set $t_1=0.$ \n\nSince $\\mathbf{v}$ is nonzero, we can pick any $t_3 \\neq 0.$ For example, setting $t_3=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v} = \\langle 0,\\, \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{4}, \\, \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{1} \\rangle.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\dfrac{b}{c} = 4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119569 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Straight Line"}] :question/id #uuid "43586a83-879c-5caf-9063-a8f4afbb8b4c" :question/math-academy-id "e-4935" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(\\sqrt{2},0,-5)$ and is perpendicular to the line\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3 \\\\ y=-1+\\sqrt{3}t \\\\ z=5-t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $\\mathbf{q}=\\langle \\sqrt{2},0,-5 \\rangle.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/assets/4c70e51d85874e5a241a5d9b35b147500d4c306187c5e0a1d15a48a9aef07706.png)\n\nThe direction vector of the line is $\\mathbf{v}=\\langle  0 , \\sqrt{3} , -1\\rangle,$ so a normal vector to the plane is \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}=\\mathbf{v}=\\langle  0 , \\sqrt{3} , -1 \\rangle.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ & =⟨\\sqrt{2},0,-5⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380192 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0d93156-f9be-5e6e-976a-bef30dc892ee" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector That Is Parallel To a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49147c48-3c79-59ef-85df-0ae687ad910c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380194} {:answer/id #uuid "43c20240-428f-5295-ac13-745401af8941" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380195} {:answer/id #uuid "b39fbfd4-ff69-5b93-9537-86630db7fb44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380196} {:answer/id #uuid "5b1511a1-0592-5e16-ae3d-355dbe352c92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380197} {:answer/id #uuid "aed5ce7a-ce77-563e-a120-802fb7c3c0e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b39fbfd4-ff69-5b93-9537-86630db7fb44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380196} :answer-field/id #uuid "51cbf961-880f-5565-ab09-ae794ec61fcf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380193}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "401ba6bc-fa27-5ba0-acab-8c53d45558b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-127873" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨0,\\,b,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩=7.$ What is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩=7$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-3,1,-2⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ -3{t}_{1}+{t}_{2}-2{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{3}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{3}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380206 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Straight Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06b379fd-7d70-5e49-8081-a3b64f84134e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,4⟩=11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380208} {:answer/id #uuid "0d2c1c27-eb96-5b3b-9be4-85fc3ed5d870" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-4,-4,3⟩=11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380209} {:answer/id #uuid "18790217-0164-5be5-8309-2e02c079a999" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,4,4⟩=23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380210} {:answer/id #uuid "56439333-b485-5577-b3fc-2b0a4fb30508" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-4,3,4⟩=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380211} {:answer/id #uuid "0677a85c-be73-579f-a4cd-3b2a328033da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩=23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380212}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0677a85c-be73-579f-a4cd-3b2a328033da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩=23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380212} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ea1771e-337a-53ba-af67-134749c7dc53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380207}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5fb6c451-3fd1-5933-bfd5-1dcab52c2777" :question/math-academy-id "q-127927" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(1,-2,3)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(4,1,-3)$ and $B(7,-3,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨1,-2,3⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(4,1,-3)$ and $B(7,-3,1)$, we can find a vector that is parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨7,-3,1⟩-⟨4,1,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-4,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨3,-4,4⟩.$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩ & =⟨1,-2,3⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩ & =23.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380213 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Straight Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24d09d6d-587a-5131-bf7b-17c4a5299f8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-6,4,5⟩=28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380215} {:answer/id #uuid "97b1a154-e6ea-5ad5-bc67-985ac790249f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨6,5,-4⟩=24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380216} {:answer/id #uuid "c19bf435-7bb8-561f-ba12-0c791dd434be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨4,-5,6⟩=-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380217} {:answer/id #uuid "6397ae12-fbfa-5ef2-932b-49e1d8b15ea1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩=-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380218} {:answer/id #uuid "facf8c4b-8e3d-5a24-a63e-b12fc172190e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-5,6,4⟩=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6397ae12-fbfa-5ef2-932b-49e1d8b15ea1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩=-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380218} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c8d44ee-444f-5365-a1c8-4d6392e75dfb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380214}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0063bd61-9495-5b7f-ae6d-384a92c58a15" :question/math-academy-id "q-127948" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(-3,2,1)$ and is  perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+6t \\\\ y=3-5t \\\\ z=-2+4t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨-3,2,1⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+6t \\\\ y=3-5t \\\\ z=-2+4t\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨-1,3,-2⟩+t\\text{ }{{⟨6,-5,4⟩}_{⏟}}_{v}.\n$$\n\n   \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨6,-5,4⟩.$ So, a normal  vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨6,-5,4⟩.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩ & =⟨-3,2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩ & =-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120149 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f5c9c30-1745-5986-b116-e9e70a7c6161" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd3ca665-8e71-5e54-9b16-e70f093f728c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r \\cdot ⟨2,-5, 3⟩ = ⟨ - 1, 2,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117415} {:answer/id #uuid "fb91c921-4313-5a71-89d6-40d058571b0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r \\cdot ⟨ - 1, 2,-3⟩ = ⟨ - 2, 5,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117416} {:answer/id #uuid "1481757a-84a9-529c-9199-edf6ab25fabd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r \\cdot ⟨ - 1, 2,-3⟩ =-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117417} {:answer/id #uuid "1e422098-0791-5c2d-bf3b-caa10d3e2a60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r \\cdot ⟨2,-5, 3⟩ = 21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117418} {:answer/id #uuid "7503109f-7701-5a9e-a969-13e4d39ac6ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r \\cdot ⟨ - 1, 2,-3⟩ =-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117419}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7503109f-7701-5a9e-a969-13e4d39ac6ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r \\cdot ⟨ - 1, 2,-3⟩ =-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117419} :answer-field/id #uuid "abbeddc4-b3d9-5bc5-9a20-fe79cc8de6b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117414}] :question/id #uuid "965706e8-86b7-56ea-92d3-d6b5a93e54f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-32971" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $P(2,-5, 3)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n = ⟨ - 1, 2,-3⟩$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316917 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f5c9c30-1745-5986-b116-e9e70a7c6161" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43c7d742-9499-5f29-91d2-b9920fb9a36c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316919} {:answer/id #uuid "d65e7cbe-fab5-5020-ae76-91046be0e73a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316920} {:answer/id #uuid "e76958a4-f0a9-564b-b572-e6bb6c971a20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316921} {:answer/id #uuid "83cfbb99-4e21-5151-9ce0-5c9a0b8bd96a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316922} {:answer/id #uuid "a7902d5d-7344-529d-a001-8ae963229f7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7902d5d-7344-529d-a001-8ae963229f7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316923} :answer-field/id #uuid "35db1012-2955-55e0-8997-945a65a2c3e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316918}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "36530b79-821b-5731-b1ff-cff3103bd6a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-33027" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $Q(1,2,-1)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $n=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes though the point $Q({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-q)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $q$ is the position vector of $Q.$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316931 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f5c9c30-1745-5986-b116-e9e70a7c6161" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72a19bb8-0aca-580c-afa4-03b4ac9e35f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,2,2⟩=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316933} {:answer/id #uuid "ae1fe646-46cf-51c7-9b0e-f0d83b96bee6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,2,3⟩=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316934} {:answer/id #uuid "732176b2-44ae-5a70-b2eb-af7b8907e33d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,3,2⟩=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316935} {:answer/id #uuid "5376dab4-36c0-5cb9-9c8a-6145e85d5897" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,3,3⟩=⟨3,2,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316936} {:answer/id #uuid "17400030-8ff4-574f-b581-15a6623c0e17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,3,3⟩=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae1fe646-46cf-51c7-9b0e-f0d83b96bee6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,2,3⟩=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316934} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6216fdb-ceae-536b-bdf2-c5cf55b5a6b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316932}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a59a738a-2841-5e3f-b750-020d46e95380" :question/math-academy-id "q-33312" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $Q(3,2,2)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨2,2,3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨3,2,2⟩,$ $n=⟨2,2,3⟩$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes though the point $Q({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-q)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $q$ is the position vector of $Q.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,2,3⟩ & =⟨3,2,2⟩\\cdot ⟨2,2,3⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,2,3⟩ & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327843 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Straight Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c44dd24-9762-5b0f-b8c3-c517b9b60ba1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩=⟨1,-4,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327845} {:answer/id #uuid "36d4f699-5e4c-578c-81de-dd6dc5597532" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩=-23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327846} {:answer/id #uuid "17782156-c5bc-52bc-b35a-443a7c32e894" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-4,2⟩=-23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327847} {:answer/id #uuid "e4f58c9a-fc06-5d06-ba42-d722b09b44a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327848} {:answer/id #uuid "1ef10d49-a269-52f1-b2ec-680de72f81b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-4,2⟩=⟨-1,5,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36d4f699-5e4c-578c-81de-dd6dc5597532" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩=-23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327846} :answer-field/id #uuid "d05dd2c3-a082-50ce-aad1-f27b3c1cd170" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327844}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b72bbef8-b4f4-5c9e-9fbc-de2a30c271f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-33317" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(1,-4,2)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(2,1,-3)$ and $B(1,6,-4).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨1,-4,2⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(2,1,-3)$ and $B(1,6,-4)$ we can find a vector parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨1,6,-4⟩-⟨2,1,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,5,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-1,5,-1⟩.$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩ & =⟨1,-4,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩ & =-23.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120181 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0d93156-f9be-5e6e-976a-bef30dc892ee" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector That Is Parallel To a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8774269b-3079-5838-8e20-b63286c329a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117607} {:answer/id #uuid "8c24e893-0b40-5d3f-a998-dcb0ba36e49d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117608} {:answer/id #uuid "1c742a2e-7c7b-58b7-bcc1-018a1b4c0473" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117609} {:answer/id #uuid "7698e5e6-2811-503f-b463-d209ca3b1a58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117610} {:answer/id #uuid "7a04dcae-4de5-5376-bea3-a84f508e95ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a04dcae-4de5-5376-bea3-a84f508e95ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117611} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bd8acfb-e547-539e-b562-9ee71ef61e78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117606}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d32af589-36a2-5da2-a4fd-d2edd8386949" :question/math-academy-id "q-33319" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,b,\\,0⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩=-14.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩=-14$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨6,-2,0⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩ & =0 \\\\ 6{t}_{1}-2{t}_{2} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =3{t}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},3{t}_{1},{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the third component of $v$ eqauls $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{3}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{1}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{1}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨1,\\,3,\\,0⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{1}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316973 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Straight Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "295f1e58-4a16-5d5a-b676-984818a41fed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316975} {:answer/id #uuid "7c31152e-66dd-5fe9-9562-96be7263d661" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,-1⟩=⟨1,1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316976} {:answer/id #uuid "4ea2f177-4c47-5d19-aa6d-d0bf73033d47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩=⟨2,1,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316977} {:answer/id #uuid "e4b58dd1-3b24-551d-b476-8762f33d28b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,-1⟩=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316978} {:answer/id #uuid "7bd83c0d-0368-5584-91e4-39648a268e3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316979}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "295f1e58-4a16-5d5a-b676-984818a41fed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316975} :answer-field/id #uuid "475d5cee-306a-5cd5-b998-795c7327de73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316974}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "be607052-6286-5c45-a7b0-2a7d8e65a24b" :question/math-academy-id "q-70892" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(2,1,-1)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(2,1,0)$ and $B(3,2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨2,1,-1⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(2,1,0)$ and $B(3,2,1)$ we can find a vector parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨3,2,1⟩-⟨2,1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨1,1,1⟩.$ \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩ & =⟨2,1,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩ & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316980 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Straight Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d60438d6-b5d2-5d15-a6df-28caf621fd6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,3⟩=⟨1,-1,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316982} {:answer/id #uuid "1a565adb-24d5-50e4-bd12-79c885a09448" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,3⟩=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316983} {:answer/id #uuid "8f485774-81e4-5a79-8ff4-16967d44158f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=⟨2,1,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316984} {:answer/id #uuid "6e428b4b-90f7-5cf9-9afd-0db57fee9352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316985} {:answer/id #uuid "9d342947-b3e8-545a-9175-0c68e2ab18bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e428b4b-90f7-5cf9-9afd-0db57fee9352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316985} :answer-field/id #uuid "427df2f4-3901-5a58-af18-9a4b43dba7bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316981}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "836af849-3232-5f71-9fa9-a73d0d879982" :question/math-academy-id "q-70894" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(2,1,-3)$ and is  perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1+t \\\\ y=2-t \\\\ z=3+2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨2,1,-3⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1+t \\\\ y=2-t \\\\ z=3+2t\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨1,2,3⟩+t\\text{ }{{⟨1,-1,2⟩}_{⏟}}_{v}.\n$$\n\n   \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨1,-1,2⟩.$ So, a normal  vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨1,-1,2⟩.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ & =⟨2,1,-3⟩\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
